# Co-processor firmware of the tablet (docs/gts7l.md §3, §13): nothing of it is in our system or
# vendor images. /mnt/vendor/firmware is the gts7l_fw logical partition (fstab.gts7l), made by
# tools/gts7l-firmware.sh from the tablet's own stock data and added to super by
# tools/gts7l-image.sh. It holds every file under the name the kernel requests:
#
#   qcom/a650_{sqe.fw,gmu.bin}, ath11k/QCA6390/hw2.0/*, qca/htbtfw20.tlv, qca/htnv20.bin,
#   cirrus/cs35l41-*        real files: only the stock vendor (which our super replaces) had
#                           them; the amp calibration is made from sec_efs
#   qcom/sm8250/..., ipa_*  symlinks into /mnt/vendor/apnhlos/image (ADSP, CDSP, SLPI, Venus,
#                           GPU zap, IPA), so those are still read from apnhlos itself
#   gts7l/{apnhlos,modem,vendor}  links to the partitions and our /vendor/firmware
#
# MANIFEST.tsv at its root lists each file, its source and the driver that loads it.
#
# This file sorts before init.gts7l.rc, so its "on fs" runs before that file's mount_all, which
# mounts the partition here; init.gts7l.rc loads the kernel modules only after that mount.

on early-init
    # The kernel loads from here. Its built-in command line (CONFIG_CMDLINE_FORCE in
    # tools/gts7l-kernel.sh's config) may name another path; the parameter is writable.
    write /sys/module/firmware_class/parameters/path /mnt/vendor/firmware

on fs
    mkdir /mnt/vendor/firmware 0755 root root
